{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEEpXH8QsDhF5RjpD86S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `closeDb()` to `src/db.ts`. It closes the Postgres pool so test suites can shut down cleanly. I haven't type-checked or run it, because the demo has no `node_modules` installed.\n\n**Why it's not the obvious one-liner:** my first try was `await db.$client.end()`. The landmine hook blocked it, citing drizzle-orm#3402: in drizzle-orm 0.36.0 (the version this project uses), `$client` may not expose `end()` in its types. The fix suggested in that issue is a `// @ts-expect-error`, which would hide the type error instead of fixing it. So I took the other route the issue mentions:\n\n- I create a `pg.Pool` directly (`pg` is already a dependency) and pass it to `drizzle(pool)`.\n- `closeDb()` calls `await pool.end()`, which is fully typed.\n\nThe connection string and its default are the same as before.\n\n**Separate problem I noticed but didn't change:** `findUser` uses `db.query.users`, but `drizzle()` is never given the schema. That means `db.query.users` will be undefined when the code runs, both before and after my change. Passing it in with `drizzle(pool, { schema: { users } })` would fix it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":744,"cache_read_input_tokens":34725,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":744},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a1a9581-4060-45f9-8bb3-6b57a14a1ac8","uuid":"18b09b6b-69f8-4d93-9c39-9bc67eec1d71","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:58:56.196Z","request_id":"req_011CgEEpWuZFUHaNZ9DPeQH7"}
